              "lean": "Finite-dimensional complete real Hilbert space E with its actual inner product and Borel measurable structure, including dimension zero; gamma is the canonical covariance-identity standard Gaussian.\nActual globally L-Lipschitz f:E->R with NNReal L>=0 including zero; every signed t in R. No differentiability, boundedness, given mean, positive dimension or concentration/LSI/domain certificate.\nFor every globally L-Lipschitz scalar observable on the stated finite real Hilbert/Borel space, its actual standard Gaussian centered exponential integral is at most exp(L^2*t^2/2) for every signed real t. Actual first moments and all exponential domains are produced by the existing shared domain theorem; the C1 restriction used inside the proof is removed internally.",
